    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is primed for a high-output slate, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (81.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.42), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Young. The 4.79 xERA of the opposing starter, coupled with helpful wind conditions, elevates both to elite status. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.96) also commands attention as a premium start, utilizing a robust dynamic platoon advantage against Martinez to secure his spot as our top UTIL play. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) continues to be a cornerstone for our stolen base production; his leadoff role and solid underlying metrics against Montero make him a high-floor selection for our lineup stability.\n\nWhile the core is set, we narrowly opted to bench **Nasim Nunez** (49.49). Despite his elite ability to hunt stolen bases, his projection suffered from a bottom-of-the-order placement and a lower aggregate efficiency score compared to our starting middle infielders, **Jacob Wilson** and **Curtis Mead**. We also monitored **Coby Mayo** (39.73), who fell just below our performance floor; a combination of a tough matchup against Sheehan and poor park factors left him on the outside looking in. Managers should keep a close watch on **Jackson Merrill** (57.31); while his profile is strong, the threat of Eovaldi\u2019s elite ability to control the running game poses a slight risk to his contribution ceiling in the SB category. Overall, with **Luis Robert Jr.** still sidelined, we are relying on the heavy hitting of **Kyle Tucker** and the dynamic speed of **Sam Antonacci** to carry the offensive load today.",
